        "title": "Introduction",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>The <strong>product rule for radicals</strong> states that the square root of a product equals the product of the square roots:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\eqalign{\n\\sqrt{a} \\cdot \\sqrt{b} = \\sqrt{ab}\n}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "The product rule for radicals states that the square root of a product equals the product of the square roots:\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n\\sqrt{a} \\cdot \\sqrt{b} = \\sqrt{ab}\n}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We can use the product rule to combine radical expressions. </p>",
            "readable_text": "We can use the product rule to combine radical expressions.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>For example, let&#x27;s suppose we want to combine the radicals in the following expression:</p>",
            "readable_text": "For example, let's suppose we want to combine the radicals in the following expression:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\sqrt{5x} \\cdot \\sqrt{6z}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \\sqrt{5x} \\cdot \\sqrt{6z}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To combine the radicals, we apply the product rule as follows:</p>",
            "readable_text": "To combine the radicals, we apply the product rule as follows:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: sqrt(5x) \u22c5 sqrt(6z)|=; sqrt(5x \u22c5 6z)|=; sqrt(30xz)]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: sqrt(5x) \u22c5 sqrt(6z)|=; sqrt(5x \u22c5 6z)|=; sqrt(30xz)]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nThe product rule for radicals states that the square root of a product equals the product of the square roots:\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n\\sqrt{a} \\cdot \\sqrt{b} = \\sqrt{ab}\n}]\n\nContent:\nWe can use the product rule to combine radical expressions.\n\nContent:\nFor example, let's suppose we want to combine the radicals in the following expression:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\sqrt{5x} \\cdot \\sqrt{6z}]\n\nContent:\nTo combine the radicals, we apply the product rule as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: sqrt(5x) \u22c5 sqrt(6z)|=; sqrt(5x \u22c5 6z)|=; sqrt(30xz)]"
      },
